{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-d104bf7fc6dca65cff34","statement":"Let $(f_0: X_0\\to Y_0)\\in \\bfC_{\\horiz}$. Assume that\n\n- for any of its base change $f:X\\to Y$, the functor $f\\horizl$ admits a continuous right adjoint $f\\horizr=(f\\horizl)^R$.\n\nUnder this assumption, and given a Cartesian diagram <<ref:eq:base-change-diagram-app>>, we further assume that\n\n[resume]\n\n- for $g\\in \\bfC_{\\verti}$, the natural Beck-Chevalley map is an isomorphism $g\\vertl\\circ (f')\\horizr\\cong f\\horizr\\circ (g')\\vertl$;\n\n- for $g\\in \\bfC_{\\horiz}$, the natural Beck-Chevalley map is an isomorphism $g\\horizl\\circ f\\horizr\\cong (f')\\horizr\\circ (g')\\horizl$;\n\n- for $\\mF\\in \\der(X)$, $\\mG\\in \\der(Z)$ we have the natural isomorphism (which is the adjunction of <<ref:eq:abstract-exterioir-pullback>>) $f\\horizr(\\mF)\\boxtimes_{\\La} \\mG \\cong (f\\times\\id)\\horizr(\\mF\\boxtimes_{\\La} \\mG)$.","source_id":"arXiv:2504.07482","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"7ac00e83e9c50d8d1c32003d1af23d96816e6aa99df86c759b6c65bb9ef9b205","kind":"result","label":"Result 562","ref_key":"assumptions.base.change.sheaf.theory.H","name":"","order":802,"deps":[{"ref":"eq:abstract-exterioir-pullback","card_id":"ma-c-cef05b4f761597d8775d","label":"Equation abstract-exterioir-pullback","resolved":true,"target":"card"},{"ref":"eq:base-change-diagram-app","card_id":"ma-c-06bece2424160671330e","label":"Equation base-change-diagram-app","resolved":true,"target":"card"}],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.07482","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"1b700e8c4a2fc6f0c0f522039f223820ba6737a9a0ac91aea37c58ba7a3389c2","line":15547,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-28T11:10:54+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v3","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":802,"math_hints":76}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:2504.07482","title":"Tame categorical local Langlands correspondence","abstract":"In one of our previous articles, we outlined the formulation of a version of the categorical arithmetic local Langlands conjecture. The aims of this article are threefold. First, we provide a detailed account of one component of this conjecture: the local Langlands category. Second, we aim to prove this conjecture in the tame case for quasi-split unramified reductive groups. Finally, we will explore the first applications of such categorical equivalence.","authors":["Xinwen Zhu"],"year":"2025","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.07482","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"fraka":"{\\mathfrak a}","frakb":"{\\mathfrak b}","frakc":"{\\mathfrak c}","frakg":"{\\mathfrak g}","frakh":"{\\mathfrak h}","frakm":"{\\mathfrak m}","frakp":"{\\mathfrak p}","fraks":"{\\mathfrak s}","frakt":"{\\mathfrak t}","fraku":"{\\mathfrak u}","frakA":"{\\mathfrak A}","frakC":"{\\mathfrak C}","frakM":"{\\mathfrak M}","frakX":"{\\mathfrak X}","bA":"{\\mathbb A}","bB":"{\\mathbb B}","bC":"{\\mathbb C}","bD":"{\\mathbb D}","bF":"{\\mathbb F}","bG":"{\\mathbb G}","bL":"{\\mathbb L}","bN":"{\\mathbb N}","bO":"{\\mathbb O}","bP":"{\\mathbb P}","bQ":"{\\mathbb Q}","bR":"{\\mathbb R}","bT":"{\\mathbb T}","bX":"{\\mathbb X}","bZ":"{\\mathbb Z}","bfA":"{\\mathbf A}","bfB":"{\\mathbf B}","bfC":"{\\mathbf C}","bfD":"{\\mathbf D}","bfE":"{\\mathbf E}","bfF":"{\\mathbf F}","bfG":"{\\mathbf G}","bfH":"{\\mathbf H}","bfI":"{\\mathbf I}","bfK":"{\\mathbf K}","bfL":"{\\mathbf L}","bfM":"{\\mathbf M}","bfN":"{\\mathbf N}","bfP":"{\\mathbf P}","bfR":"{\\mathbf R}","bfS":"{\\mathbf S}","bfT":"{\\mathbf T}","bfa":"{\\mathbf a}","bff":"{\\mathbf f}","mA":"{\\mathcal A}","mB":"{\\mathcal B}","mE":"{\\mathcal E}","mF":"{\\mathcal F}","mG":"{\\mathcal G}","mH":"{\\mathcal H}","mI":"{\\mathcal I}","mJ":"{\\mathcal J}","mK":"{\\mathcal K}","mL":"{\\mathcal L}","mM":"{\\mathcal M}","mN":"{\\mathcal N}","mO":"{\\mathcal O}","mP":"{\\ma